.git
.github
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
pytest.log
# The release pin, kept OUT of the artefact it names. A digest is recorded
# after the push, so an image built at one release would carry the digests of
# the previous one — a file inside the artefact making a stale claim about
# which artefact it is. A run reads its image from WOMBLEX_IMAGE_REF, injected
# by the deployment; nothing in the image reads this file.
deploy/
output/
# ...but keep the vendored demo corpus: `womblex seed-demo` publishes it into a
# fresh console's store, and both Dockerfiles rely on `COPY . /app` carrying it
# to /app/output/console-demo (see store/demo_corpus.py).
!output/console-demo/
.venv/
venv/
# Local development virtualenvs (e.g. `.venv-312`, `.venv-test`). Never belong
# in the image and, unignored, dominate the build context (multi-GB) — the
# same reason `.venv/` above is excluded. Kept broad so any `.venv*` variant a
# contributor creates stays out.
.venv*/
**/.venv*/
# Benchmark fixtures are large and not needed in the runtime image.
fixtures/fixtures/
docs/accuracy/
*.egg-info/
# A stamp left by a local `python -m build` names whatever commit that build
# saw. The image writes its own after install (or honestly reports none), so
# keeping a work tree's out of the context is what stops a stale commit riding
# in and being believed.
src/womblex/_build_stamp.py
# Built by Dockerfile.ui's frontend-builder stage, not the base build context.
ui/node_modules/
ui/build/
ui/.svelte-kit/
